# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the op-fusion SHIP gates (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of
# tp4/fusion-1 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. Templates only: no tag is pushed from the
# branch by its author. ORDER.txt has the order, the stop rules, the minutes and the pass rule. ONE IMAGE: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-s6nt-1 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag B0 builds from the approved commit
# (sed -i 's/tp4-s6nt-1/<tag>/' *.env). The cards are under development: nothing here stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
# SR (STOP) RUNS ON THE BASE VARIANT OF THE THIN LAYER, NEVER ON THE PRODUCTION LAYER: the four-card platform replay, the node agent's serving sequence
# (c2_platform_replay.py) in a copy of its container, running the thin layer built on the B0 image WITHOUT the production layer's checkpoint lines: no QWEN_C2_MODEL_REPO,
# no QWEN_C2_MODEL_REVISION, and the Dockerfile's own alias Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B:tt in place of ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b:tt (C2_PLATFORM_IMAGE=local:thin-layer: the step
# reads the image name from a file the operator writes on the runner; it is never committed). WHY: the replay step loads the checkpoint the replay names (serving.manage
# --model, the base's: the workflow passes no other and this reader refuses C2_MODEL_REPO and C2_MODEL_REVISION beside a replay), and on a layer that selects
# ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b the contract refuses a platform model naming the base (check_platform_model: the API server exits 78 at every load); the replay's served-name
# check defaults to the base's alias, and the runtime's compiled per-model kwargs (the reasoning and tool-call parsers) name the base only (production's checkpoint takes
# its parsers from its library entry at the deploy). BUILD the production layer as the base variant plus ONE layer of those three ENV lines and nothing else, and compare
# the sorted Config.Env of the two images: they differ by exactly those three lines. SR therefore qualifies the platform sequence (release-first load, warm-up, coding, four
# concurrent requests, a tool call, the traffic steps, the in-place reload, the stop and start) and the B0 image's bytes ON THE BASE CHECKPOINT, not the production bytes:
# the production layer is first served by the library deploy (release_first), and its post-deploy read is /v1/models naming ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b:tt, a tool call
# answered as tool_calls, the reasoning split, and this pack's no-tier read in the engine log. The replay hands its container no profile: C2_REPLAY_PROFILE (required on
# four cards) is the profile the image must boot BY ITS DEFAULT, and every boot must log it, which is why SR needs the baked B0 image and so the APPROVED decision. THE
# RECORDED SOURCE: the step looks for the base's placement container by name and, with production unserved, falls back to the tracked record of the base's placement
# (scripts/ci/references/c2-serving: its checkpoint is the base's, as the base variant serves); to subtract that record's source image ENV it needs the source image present
# on the rig host (c2_platform_replay.source_problem): when the step reports 'the source image ... is not on this host', the operator pulls it first - the image name stays
# out of this file. The base's own converted weights are read at the first load (the base's unkeyed weight cache, which the base's placements built); a cold one is
# converted at that load, an ESTIMATED 8 to 25 minutes (docs/tp4-swift.md) that can outlast the replay's startup wait, so the operator confirms it is on the hub before the
# window. READ the vLLM subprocess log: '[QWEN-C2] profile c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-traffic-s6-nt: vLLM argv', the OWNER TRAFFIC WAIVER line, the
# P150x4 mesh, admission passed with no UNQUALIFIED admission line and no 262k evidence waiver, prefix installed, the Lever N install and warm lines, the parked build line,
# every op-fusion lever's engaged line, the Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B:tt alias before and after the restart, and no kill-switch line (no levern.off, prefix-reuse.off or parked.off
# left on the hub). PASS: 'PLATFORM_REPLAY passed=True'. The replay turns the session cap off; the cap is read live after the deploy. The replay step has no telemetry
# sidecar. Measured basis: 25 minutes. NO-TIER READ (tp4/s6-notier): no "host tier on" line and no "host tier restore slice on" line; the checkpoint store at 16 GiB; the
# "[PINDIAG] text-only boot: vision tower skipped" line once per engine process and no vision weight load in the boot log; the "[PINDIAG] host heap trimmed after warmup"
# line once (or its skipped line, never a traceback); every other ship-6 read unchanged (the governor's install line, WC's engaged line and its one octo decline). Duration
# (estimate): 30 minutes.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset replay
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-s6nt-1
C2_PLATFORM_IMAGE=local:thin-layer
C2_REPLAY_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-traffic-s6-nt
C2_BOX_MINUTES=60
